# Reference databases are LF on every platform.
#
# Git already stores these files as LF. This makes Windows checkouts write LF too
# (with core.autocrlf=true they would otherwise be CRLF), so a clone matches the
# released bytes and the Zenodo SHA-256 checksums, and a CRLF file written by R on
# Windows is committed as LF. Only FASTA and TSV are covered; CSV, R, Rmd, md and
# html files are left as they are.
*.fasta text eol=lf
*.tsv   text eol=lf
